07:04.820 --> 07:05.640
Kuga-san?

07:05.960 --> 07:07.570
Are you dizzy from the heat?

07:07.570 --> 07:10.270
No, I'm fine. It's nothing.

07:10.270 --> 07:11.290
Kuga-san?

07:11.860 --> 07:13.470
I'm fine!

07:12.730 --> 07:14.450
What're they doing?

07:13.470 --> 07:14.660
Are you sure?

07:19.200 --> 07:20.810
What a feast!

07:38.590 --> 07:41.940
<i>They said </i>they<i> were going 
to use the footbath, too.</i>

07:44.180 --> 07:46.440
May I sit next to you?

07:46.440 --> 07:48.950
Yeah. Sure. Of course.

07:52.530 --> 07:54.890
Kuga-san, I...

07:55.990 --> 07:58.160
There's something I want to do with you.

07:59.440 --> 08:00.700
<i>So cute!</i>

08:02.580 --> 08:06.720
Look at this, I installed 
manga production software!

08:06.720 --> 08:08.700
A drawing app!

08:10.060 --> 08:12.580
Oh, right. That.

08:12.580 --> 08:15.780
Once you're used to it, it's not much 
different from drawing on paper.

08:15.780 --> 08:16.620
See?

08:16.620 --> 08:20.840
I haven't touched this sort of thing 
since I deleted Moka-nee's data.

08:20.840 --> 08:23.210
It's just doodling for fun.

08:23.210 --> 08:25.880
See, you can even redo things.

08:26.310 --> 08:28.100
And applying tone is a cinch.

08:28.710 --> 08:30.830
Give it a try, Kuga-san.

08:30.830 --> 08:31.600
Sure.

08:36.870 --> 08:39.310
Wow, that really is something.

08:39.310 --> 08:44.050
And if you take the wonderful art this 
kind person made, and do this...

08:45.270 --> 08:47.410
These days, you can even do stuff like that?

08:48.710 --> 08:50.840
Now I'm interested.

08:50.840 --> 08:51.870
I thought you might be.

08:52.140 --> 08:54.030
It's good for adding color, too.

09:01.170 --> 09:05.240
We've come to this great place 
with an incredible view,

09:05.240 --> 09:07.050
yet we're playing around with a tablet.

09:07.050 --> 09:09.290
Well, good point.

09:09.290 --> 09:11.640
I've never had a New Year like this.

09:12.420 --> 09:13.650
I'm truly grateful.

09:16.860 --> 09:21.190
What a relief. It kind of seemed 
like you were avoiding eye contact.

09:21.190 --> 09:24.530
N-No, I was just being self-conscious...

09:24.530 --> 09:25.940
Sorry.

09:25.940 --> 09:28.670
Is that what it was? Gee.

09:29.200 --> 09:32.670
I've never spent New Year's like this either,

09:32.670 --> 09:36.380
and it's fun, but I've also had some doubts.

09:36.780 --> 09:38.790
It's okay to enjoy it, isn't it?

09:38.790 --> 09:40.140
Goshiki-san.

09:40.720 --> 09:43.270
It worries you that you didn't go home, huh?

09:44.800 --> 09:48.760
The truth is, I left the island 
without my mother's permission.

09:48.760 --> 09:54.550
I managed to leave thanks to my grandmother's
 dying wish that I get to do what I want.

09:55.050 --> 09:57.750
And your mother isn't too pleased.

09:57.750 --> 10:03.210
It was my first time ever disobeying her, so 
it felt like my heart was going to burst!

10:04.950 --> 10:06.930
Oh, I'm sorry!

10:06.930 --> 10:10.200
Here we are on this trip, 
and we're talking about this!

10:10.390 --> 10:11.610
It's not like that!

10:11.610 --> 10:15.930
Well, that is, I don't mean you 
should force yourself to cheer up.

10:15.930 --> 10:18.400
I realize you're concerned about the island,

10:18.400 --> 10:23.190
but also don't want to go back, 
so it's okay for you to worry.

10:24.120 --> 10:26.420
It's hard to put into words,

10:26.420 --> 10:28.590
but if the island's weighing on your mind,

10:28.590 --> 10:33.330
I just wish there was a way for you to feel 
better without necessarily going back.

10:33.330 --> 10:36.130
And I wonder what I can do about it.

10:46.880 --> 10:50.050
G-Goshiki-san! Um...

10:50.050 --> 10:52.990
I feel better about it now.

10:52.990 --> 10:54.260
Why?

10:56.370 --> 10:59.310
Because you know the way I feel.

11:02.890 --> 11:03.670
Yeah.

11:15.620 --> 11:17.860
I slept so much!

11:17.860 --> 11:18.980
Good morning.

11:18.980 --> 11:22.000
Good morning. You got up early.

11:22.000 --> 11:25.740
Yeah, I was too wound up to sleep much.

11:27.120 --> 11:28.980
Kinda like a little kid.

11:31.130 --> 11:32.970
What are you looking at?

11:35.230 --> 11:38.360
The photos from yesterday.
 I sure did take a lot of them.

11:45.200 --> 11:48.670
They're lovely! Could you send them to me?

11:48.670 --> 11:50.140
Of course.

11:50.140 --> 11:51.870
Thank you.

11:53.880 --> 11:56.320
Goshiki-san? You okay?

11:59.320 --> 12:02.860
Incoming call

11:59.320 --> 12:02.860
Mother

12:03.360 --> 12:05.570
Incoming call

12:03.360 --> 12:05.570
Mother

12:07.900 --> 12:10.570
Uh, would you mind listening in?

12:11.950 --> 12:12.840
All right.

12:14.640 --> 12:15.740
Hello.

12:15.740 --> 12:17.090
<i>Are you doing well?</i>

12:17.090 --> 12:20.570
No need to worry, Mother. 
There's no problem.

12:20.570 --> 12:22.830
<i>You haven't contacted us at all.</i>

12:22.830 --> 12:24.090
Well...

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Mother

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Ongoing call

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Mute

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Speakerphone

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Video call

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
Contacts

12:24.090 --> 12:29.850
<i>How worried do you imagine we've been 
while you've been living carefree?</i>

12:29.850 --> 12:32.090
I <i>am</i> sorry about that.

12:32.090 --> 12:35.100
Your entire life is here and only here.

12:37.110 --> 12:40.850
There are also people 
here who care about me!

12:40.850 --> 12:42.770
Even one whom I'm dating!

12:44.160 --> 12:45.100
<i>I said it...</i>

12:46.240 --> 12:47.850
Good morning!

12:47.850 --> 12:49.760
My name is Ichiro Kuga!

12:49.760 --> 12:53.350
I'm in a serious relationship 
with Goshiki-san!

12:53.350 --> 12:55.240
And so, it's nice to meet you!

13:00.240 --> 13:01.750
S-Sorry!

13:01.750 --> 13:04.740
I guess I couldn't stand 
what she said to you!

13:05.670 --> 13:09.020
I wanted to tell her you're 
more loved than that...

13:09.020 --> 13:11.740
<i>Man</i>, I should have been calmer!

13:11.740 --> 13:15.380
For the future's sake, I'd better 
offer her a more proper greeting!

13:19.520 --> 13:20.970
Goshiki-san?

13:25.180 --> 13:27.780
I am loved, aren't I?

13:34.150 --> 13:35.750
You got that right!

13:35.750 --> 13:38.050
I don't know what's going on, but yay!

13:39.190 --> 13:41.250
Thanks for being patient!

13:41.250 --> 13:42.470
Let's head on out.

13:42.470 --> 13:43.600
Okay!

14:00.290 --> 14:02.070
I-I'm taking it.

14:02.070 --> 14:02.940
Okay.

14:05.370 --> 14:08.210
Shio-chan, take a picture!

14:08.210 --> 14:09.610
All right!

14:14.090 --> 14:16.740
I'm in a serious relationship 
with Goshiki-san!

14:17.260 --> 14:22.470
<i>What if what I said made things 
worse between her and her family?</i>

14:22.460 --> 14:24.460
Boat platform

14:22.680 --> 14:24.460
Hurry!

14:24.780 --> 14:29.100
<i>From their perspective, I'm some 
mystery guy who suddenly appeared</i>

14:29.100 --> 14:31.470
<i>months after their daughter went to Tokyo.</i>

14:31.470 --> 14:33.670
<i>I've done it now!</i>

14:35.010 --> 14:37.960
Ichiro! Let's take a picture together!

14:50.460 --> 14:52.240
Is it true, then?

14:52.240 --> 14:54.990
Is the princess being 
deceived by a villain?!

15:04.280 --> 15:08.500
He made some teasing mention of 
marriage and then hung up on me.

15:09.020 --> 15:11.130
Who is this guy, a con artist?

15:11.130 --> 15:13.770
They're out there, you know. 
Matrimonial swindlers!

15:13.770 --> 15:17.020
The princess is in danger.
 Let's call her home immediately.

15:17.790 --> 15:19.760
I will go and get her.

15:19.760 --> 15:21.530
You personally, Miyako-sama?

15:21.530 --> 15:24.140
You mustn't. What would become of the island?

15:24.140 --> 15:26.900
Both Star Children gone at the same time?!

15:26.900 --> 15:30.660
But do you think anyone else 
can bring back the princess?

15:30.660 --> 15:33.170
No, that would never work.

15:33.170 --> 15:36.040
But Miyako-sama, surely you won't go alone?

15:36.660 --> 15:38.540
We'll go with her.

15:38.780 --> 15:40.050
Takeru-san!

15:40.520 --> 15:42.780
I must speak to her, as her parent.

15:52.680 --> 15:53.960
Shiori...

15:56.640 --> 15:58.050
Lovely.

15:58.050 --> 16:00.360
I want us to have a matching pair.

15:58.060 --> 16:00.890
<b>Limited-edition Lake Kawaguchi key rings</b>

16:02.320 --> 16:05.860
Kuga-san, Kuga-san. 
Time to get some mementos.

16:05.860 --> 16:07.290
We're gonna go check the chocolates!

16:07.290 --> 16:08.070
Okay.

16:11.400 --> 16:12.650
Kuga-san?

16:12.650 --> 16:14.070
Oh, yeah.

16:15.940 --> 16:17.700
You're getting a call.

16:18.660 --> 16:21.390
Whatever. It's just my mother.

16:22.450 --> 16:24.410
Don't worry about it so much.

16:24.410 --> 16:25.860
I do, though!

16:27.270 --> 16:30.170
I think I made things more complicated.

16:30.170 --> 16:34.090
It had to be a surprise, me jumping 
in like that with no warning.

16:34.440 --> 16:38.110
Maybe now your relationship with 
your family is even worse.

16:38.110 --> 16:42.100
I was grateful, so please 
don't talk that way.

16:42.100 --> 16:45.360
Well, it's not like 
I wanted to pick a fight.

16:45.360 --> 16:50.120
If I'd really been thinking about you, 
I'd have known not to ramble on irresponsibly.

16:50.120 --> 16:52.010
I-Irresponsibly?

16:52.010 --> 16:55.600
Does that mean you got caught up
 in the heat of the moment?

16:55.600 --> 17:01.870
No. I've given it plenty of thought.
 I just wish I had said it more tactfully.

17:03.870 --> 17:05.380
Goshiki-san?

17:05.380 --> 17:07.560
I was very happy then.

17:07.560 --> 17:11.120
That's good enough, so you don't 
need to go regretting it!

17:11.120 --> 17:14.980
Well, it's reflection more than regret.

17:14.980 --> 17:18.190
Like, I should have thought 
harder about it for your sake.

17:18.470 --> 17:21.550
Wh-Why do you end up losing 
confidence, Kuga-san?

17:23.890 --> 17:25.310
<i>Confidence!</i>

17:25.310 --> 17:29.710
When you go red from shyness or smile 
reservedly, it really touches me!

17:29.710 --> 17:30.440
Wait—

17:30.440 --> 17:34.060
But there's no use brooding 
over what's already done!

17:34.360 --> 17:36.060
B-Brooding?

17:36.340 --> 17:39.320
Well, I happen to think so, too.

17:39.320 --> 17:44.330
What I'm trying to say is, 
you're a very lovely person!

17:45.810 --> 17:51.340
That's what you say, but I've 
never thought of myself that way.

17:51.340 --> 17:52.580
Oh, no...

17:53.600 --> 17:54.320
But—

17:54.320 --> 17:59.210
I don't want the one I love 
to look down on himself!

18:04.150 --> 18:05.850
K-Kuga-san!

18:05.850 --> 18:08.210
Are you all right, Kuga-san?!

18:08.610 --> 18:11.540
R-Retribution again.

18:11.540 --> 18:13.930
I've had about enough...

18:16.200 --> 18:20.350
<i>Oh, it's the same imagery 
as when I was first stung.</i>

18:20.690 --> 18:24.380
<i>She said then that I'd been "linked."</i>

18:26.180 --> 18:30.860
<i>Why is it the only means of 
linking has to be so sad?</i>

18:35.230 --> 18:37.690
Kuga-san, should I call someone?

18:37.690 --> 18:39.370
Maybe it's best if you keep still.

18:41.890 --> 18:44.880
It's just anemia. I'm all right.

18:44.880 --> 18:45.960
Oh.

18:46.750 --> 18:49.160
I made you angry...

18:49.160 --> 18:51.400
It's because I was sad.

18:51.700 --> 18:54.790
<i>Oh, I made her sad.</i>

18:55.230 --> 18:56.900
Sorry, Goshiki-san.

18:56.900 --> 18:58.810
No, I was the one who...

19:11.410 --> 19:13.490
D-Don't strain yourself.

19:13.490 --> 19:14.920
I'm fine!

19:15.410 --> 19:18.190
And I'm... I'm fed up with this!

19:18.190 --> 19:21.530
We can't even argue with this dumb pact.

19:21.950 --> 19:24.920
Yeah, neither of us was at fault.

19:25.270 --> 19:26.380
I know, right?!

19:30.170 --> 19:33.200
You're smiling again. What's up?

19:33.200 --> 19:35.440
You're the one this thing afflicts.

19:35.440 --> 19:37.270
Sorry, I just...

19:37.270 --> 19:39.450
I thought you were mad at me back there.

19:39.690 --> 19:41.160
I'm sad.

19:41.450 --> 19:43.520
Yeah. I know that now.

19:43.960 --> 19:47.210
I just thought, seriously 
angry people sure are pretty.

19:49.920 --> 19:53.020
This... is no time for saying such things.

19:53.020 --> 19:53.930
Sorry.

19:54.350 --> 19:57.470
I've never thought of myself as lovely.

19:57.470 --> 19:58.960
That again?

19:58.960 --> 20:03.470
But I do like myself quite 
a bit for loving you.

20:03.800 --> 20:06.710
That's why I've got so much 
rattling around in my head.

20:06.710 --> 20:07.960
Huh.

20:08.360 --> 20:11.660
All right, then. Sort out your thoughts.

20:12.430 --> 20:15.800
And please come away from 
it liking yourself a lot.

20:17.050 --> 20:18.390
Shio-chan!

20:19.260 --> 20:21.230
What's wrong, Ichiro?

20:21.230 --> 20:22.540
You okay?

20:21.240 --> 20:23.740
Lake Kawaguchi Souvenirs

20:22.540 --> 20:23.730
Ichiro.

20:23.730 --> 20:25.000
It's anemia.

20:25.000 --> 20:25.570
Huh?

20:25.570 --> 20:28.730
I got a little dizzy, but I'm fine now.

20:28.990 --> 20:29.990
Really?

20:29.990 --> 20:31.880
You bet!

20:32.140 --> 20:34.490
Well, all's well that ends well.

20:34.490 --> 20:35.760
These are for you two.

20:35.760 --> 20:36.880
These?

20:39.070 --> 20:40.670
Souvenirs for you.

20:40.670 --> 20:41.790
For you.

20:42.310 --> 20:44.210
To thank Shio-chan for the trip.

20:44.890 --> 20:47.400
Don't you like having a matching pair?

20:48.170 --> 20:50.080
Thank you!

20:50.080 --> 20:51.630
I'll treasure it for life.

20:51.630 --> 20:54.160
Whoa, don't go overboard!

20:54.160 --> 20:56.280
It makes me so happy!

20:56.280 --> 20:58.580
Maybe <i>too</i> happy!

21:00.950 --> 21:02.730
We've got to buy something for us, too!

21:04.430 --> 21:09.810
The two of us are in love, 
but we aren't all by ourselves.

21:10.740 --> 21:13.650
Not as long as we have 
Machi-chan and Fumi-kun.

21:14.670 --> 21:18.920
I feel like I understand your 
troubles a little better.

21:20.140 --> 21:22.920
Are you willing to fight by my side?

21:23.330 --> 21:27.920
It might mean going to 
the island to annul the pact.

21:28.540 --> 21:32.670
But even so, I want us to be rid 
of the pact once and for all.

21:36.840 --> 21:39.330
Yeah, let's go together.

21:45.900 --> 21:47.880
Back home already.

21:47.880 --> 21:49.330
Let's go visit again sometime.

21:50.660 --> 21:51.770
Huh?

21:51.770 --> 21:53.080
Someone's here.

21:53.440 --> 21:55.050
We have a guest?

22:01.370 --> 22:03.430
We're going home, Shiori.

22:04.130 --> 22:06.740
M-M...

22:07.850 --> 22:09.670
Mother?!

22:09.670 --> 22:11.400
"Mother"?!

22:16.060 --> 22:27.650
A long red thread stretching 
into the distance

22:27.650 --> 22:38.800
Meeting you, even if it meant having 
to cross hundreds of light-years

22:38.800 --> 22:45.480
Maybe I'll slowly get used to

22:45.480 --> 22:52.390
The two of us going out to have fun

22:52.390 --> 23:02.230
A tug on my arm, by the bond 
that was formed that day

23:02.230 --> 23:08.090
A little at a time, we've 
come closer together

23:08.090 --> 23:12.880
More smiles for us

23:12.880 --> 23:25.690
That place I first learned of, and 
the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:25.690 --> 23:31.650
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:31.650 --> 23:38.490
Looking forward to it, good night

23:45.530 --> 23:47.440
This day has finally arrived!

23:47.440 --> 23:50.830
The bigger the obstacles, 
the hotter burns the love!

23:50.830 --> 23:52.620
Don't you think you read too much manga?

23:52.620 --> 23:55.160
Come on! Overcome this obstacle with me!

23:55.160 --> 23:57.180
Even should the flames surround us!

23:56.080 --> 24:00.070
<b>Episode 10</b>

23:56.080 --> 24:00.070
<b><b>Family Meeting with the Princess</b></b>

23:57.180 --> 23:59.340
G-Goshiki-san! The flames are in your eyes!
